1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,971
Two days. On both days the market opened at the same price.

2
00:00:09,421 --> 00:00:17,857
Day one moved in one direction from morning to evening. Day two went up and down, and closed back in the middle.

3
00:00:18,308 --> 00:00:23,951
Can the first hour of the morning hint at which day it will be? That is today's topic.

4
00:00:24,951 --> 00:00:29,783
Hello, this is episode ten of the SPIDER Order Flow series.

5
00:00:30,232 --> 00:00:35,641
Last time: session profiles, a separate volume profile for each session.

6
00:00:36,091 --> 00:00:41,811
Today: Market Profile, also called TPO, and the types of days.

7
00:00:42,811 --> 00:00:51,719
A volume profile shows how much volume traded at each price. A Market Profile shows how much time was spent at each price.

8
00:00:52,169 --> 00:01:00,293
Split the day into half-hour periods. Each period gets a letter: A, B, C and so on.

9
00:01:00,743 --> 00:01:09,991
Every price touched in that half hour gets that letter. Each mark is a TPO, a Time Price Opportunity.

10
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:17,911
In 24-hour forex, pick one session, like London or New York, and count the letters from its open.

11
00:01:18,911 --> 00:01:23,274
Now slide all the letters to the left. A shape appears.

12
00:01:23,723 --> 00:01:31,535
The price with the most letters is where price spent the most time. That is the TPO point of control.

13
00:01:31,985 --> 00:01:36,347
And the zone holding about 70% of the letters is the value area.

14
00:01:37,347 --> 00:01:42,179
Where a price has just one letter, it is called a single print.

15
00:01:42,630 --> 00:01:47,226
It means price moved through quickly. Nobody stayed there.

16
00:01:47,676 --> 00:01:57,395
A tail of single prints at the top or bottom edge shows the market rejected those prices.

17
00:01:58,395 --> 00:02:01,948
Now the most important piece: the Initial Balance.

18
00:02:02,398 --> 00:02:07,804
It is the first hour's range, the high and low of the A and B periods.

19
00:02:08,255 --> 00:02:14,054
It is the day's first decision. The rest of the day is read against this range.

20
00:02:15,054 --> 00:02:21,662
If price leaves the Initial Balance after the first hour, it is called range extension.

21
00:02:22,113 --> 00:02:26,162
It means new players arrived and pushed in one direction.

22
00:02:26,612 --> 00:02:32,097
How often it extends, and in which direction, decides the type of day.

23
00:02:33,097 --> 00:02:35,370
Type one: the normal day.

24
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:41,620
The Initial Balance is wide, and price stays mostly inside it all day.

25
00:02:42,070 --> 00:02:47,712
Little or no extension. The profile is fat and full in the middle.

26
00:02:48,712 --> 00:02:51,063
Type two: the trend day.

27
00:02:51,513 --> 00:02:57,704
The Initial Balance is small, then price keeps printing new letters in one direction.

28
00:02:58,154 --> 00:03:04,423
The profile is thin and long, and the close is usually near one extreme of the day.

29
00:03:04,873 --> 00:03:09,784
The biggest mistake: fading a trend day again and again.

30
00:03:10,784 --> 00:03:15,225
Type three: the balance day, also called a neutral day.

31
00:03:15,674 --> 00:03:20,585
The Initial Balance breaks on both sides, above and below.

32
00:03:21,036 --> 00:03:25,555
But neither side holds, and the close is back in the middle.

33
00:03:26,555 --> 00:03:29,795
The open also gives an early clue about the day.

34
00:03:30,245 --> 00:03:38,447
Open drive: price moves one way right from the open and never returns to it. A strong sign.

35
00:03:38,897 --> 00:03:45,428
Open test drive: it first tests one side, then turns and drives hard the other way.

36
00:03:45,878 --> 00:03:53,767
Open rejection reverse: it goes one way, gets rejected, and comes back through the open.

37
00:03:54,216 --> 00:04:02,341
And open auction: no urgency, price rotates around the open. Often a range day.

38
00:04:03,341 --> 00:04:04,908
So, today's summary.

39
00:04:05,358 --> 00:04:14,108
TPO is a profile of time. One letter per half hour. The price with the most letters is the POC.

40
00:04:14,559 --> 00:04:22,918
The Initial Balance is the first hour's range. Extension shows the day type: normal, trend or balance.

41
00:04:23,368 --> 00:04:29,977
And the open type gives the first clue early. Not a guarantee, just a clue.

42
00:04:30,977 --> 00:04:35,575
Next episode: Time and Sales, reading the tape.

43
